{
  "dom_id": "step-835631",
  "name": "Finding Whole-Number Bounds for Roots",
  "problem": "**Bounds** are values that trap a number between a lower value and an upper value. For roots, **whole-number bounds** are consecutive whole numbers that the root lies between.\n\nTo find whole-number bounds, we compare the number under the radical to nearby perfect squares or perfect cubes.\n\nLet's locate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/dbd2aff681e9d97891999f08502f4f6e7f41f487b237d6c90e18afa1f77755ef.svg) The nearby perfect squares are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/24341571e162e3b4e2ca76590f0ed2e6d8b180365fba30c3fb9ea6041d38179a.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/3cba1142c4b937d3598aaaed096f8b95178d8c45baf39fb7f9f02f21a21480df.svg) because\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/09aad9428a24389e5a19034319e2737d08cf5167bf424e1b78cf0f0e69e49102.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/119ef80e819318a00b93e3c34aaca245545c965604be3489dd3529df1232a453.svg) is between these perfect squares, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/8fbdaf9d9bd26df7fe6d1c1ad4403f07ba47a94f1a7f8b0d4e728b6865a7cb23.svg)\n\nTaking the square root of each part gives\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/c9753a4537cde93f9b0a994a0c50bdc6528dba6926bdd021d0cc2b54732277ba.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/448579015986d36689743ffeadb6a8b05c96b917778d63a0de7e4a2dd0487370.png)\n\nSo, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/e8219f12c397796f3e761fb39940934f3f6ff51cb7dd3656018be76bcf7db1ba.svg) lies between the consecutive whole numbers ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/fe34f715005da1a8b682c9650a76785673fdf25c3b7c7546bb94824470c54caf.svg) The same idea works for cube roots, except we compare to nearby perfect cubes instead.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-835631\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"835631\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"23020\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-835631\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-2\">Finding Whole-Number Bounds for Roots</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"835631\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p><strong>Bounds</strong> are values that trap a number between a lower value and an upper value. For roots, <strong>whole-number bounds</strong> are consecutive whole numbers that the root lies between.</p>\n<p>To find whole-number bounds, we compare the number under the radical to nearby perfect squares or perfect cubes.</p>\n<p>Let's locate <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.25ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.821ex\" height=\"2.398ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -949.5 2131 1060\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><path data-c=\"33\" d=\"M127 463Q100 463 85 480T69 524Q69 579 117 622T233 665Q268 665 277 664Q351 652 390 611T430 522Q430 470 396 421T302 350L299 348Q299 347 308 345T337 336T375 315Q457 262 457 175Q457 96 395 37T238 -22Q158 -22 100 21T42 130Q42 158 60 175T105 193Q133 193 151 175T169 130Q169 119 166 110T159 94T148 82T136 74T126 70T118 67L114 66Q165 21 238 21Q293 21 321 74Q338 107 338 175V195Q338 290 274 322Q259 328 213 329L171 330L168 332Q166 335 166 348Q166 366 174 366Q202 366 232 371Q266 376 294 413T322 525V533Q322 590 287 612Q265 626 240 626Q208 626 181 615T143 592T132 580H135Q138 579 143 578T153 573T165 566T175 555T183 540T186 520Q186 498 172 481T127 463Z\"></path><path data-c=\"32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></path></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,89.5)\"><path data-c=\"221A\" d=\"M95 178Q89 178 81 186T72 200T103 230T169 280T207 309Q209 311 212 311H213Q219 311 227 294T281 177Q300 134 312 108L397 -77Q398 -77 501 136T707 565T814 786Q820 800 834 800Q841 800 846 794T853 782V776L620 293L385 -193Q381 -200 366 -200Q357 -200 354 -197Q352 -195 256 15L160 225L144 214Q129 202 113 190T95 178Z\"></path></g><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"829.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1853,0)\"><path data-c=\"2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> The nearby perfect squares are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 1000 688\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><path data-c=\"32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 4